 [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"4f6562ec25c62994d6994d57d18052b45ff53ea9985e99ddc228f1cda8b9c1e1","event_uuid":"2209c64e-08bf-4403-921a-bf079d72b4dc","position":{"commit_sha":"e90de911ca44f4eb0bcca4b5787ca8c3d5d4483a","position":"1786809762848018001-2209c64e-08bf-4403-921a-bf079d72b4dc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"11e64267232df74055d6930aa4b3edd1a196d3aec269797294b5c50e59742e9d","event_uuid":"a2755f46-5a81-42b9-a48f-458f71faefdf","position":{"commit_sha":"dcada07772903090ba70e72a96b315281d7d2d99","position":"1786810108929183001-a2755f46-5a81-42b9-a48f-458f71faefdf"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"fa674f0bffe30344de70f29e9f2b4911d6495a563abff752e483fdefb225a8a2","event_uuid":"63672381-5842-4ef2-a4a1-9fd5bca7e0fa","position":{"commit_sha":"ffa99cb28061688667be593c05dc60de359d902a","position":"1786810629337156579-63672381-5842-4ef2-a4a1-9fd5bca7e0fa"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Claimed in worktree impl-fea4-seams off origin/main (0f34e8dc3b). Plan-review PASS+signed after revising to: (1) scope projects_store standalone docstring to the read path (write path lazily imports seams), (2) preserve path.parent.mkdir before atomic_write, (3) run the RMW under lock.write_lock so the mutation is genuinely under the lock, then commit_and_push publishes. Implementing RED->GREEN next.","timestamp":1786809762848018001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed to Gerrit for review: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1813 (commit cde01d009e). Pure seam conversion complete. RED->GREEN: guard test (RMW nested in write_lock then commit_and_push_tickets_branch called with tracker) failed RED on unconverted code, passes GREEN after wiring _lib_ops mutators. Byte-identity pin passes (json.dumps indent=2 sort_keys=True + trailing newline, byte-for-byte). No seam modified; no facade/helper added (inlined the two seam call-sites). Gates from worktree: make lint PASS, make typecheck PASS (547 files), 21 projects/bridge tests PASS incl. ABSENT=legal-empty / MALFORMED=fail-closed. docs/concurrency.md records the two-part invariant. Not closing: awaits Verified +1 + LLM-Review +1.","timestamp":1786810108929183001}],"created_at":1786807588199068001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"657b4586-abde-4ea2-8aaa-14870ee4ae4b","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"05b8-4efe-8d58-4c27"},{"link_uuid":"63672381-5842-4ef2-a4a1-9fd5bca7e0fa","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6e0c-2639-3c03-417a"}],"description":"## Problem\nThe .bridge_state/projects.json write path is a HAND-ROLLED client that bypasses the\nauthoritative shared store seams and thereby violates the tickets-branch invariant\n(every mutation runs under the unified write lock AND auto-commits+publishes).\nprojects_store._write_record hand-rolls tempfile+os.replace instead of the shared\nfsutil.atomic_write, and projects_store.set_project/remove_project never take the lock,\ncommit, or push. This forced the ad-hoc hand-commits behind incident\n05b8-4efe-8d58-4c27 (LEG/ONE/TWO/ZERO leak).\n\n## Scope: CONVERT the hand-rolled client to the authoritative shared seams ONLY\nReuse the existing seams exactly as-is. Do NOT modify any seam and do NOT build a facade\nover them (that would be additional, separately-approved scope):\n- rebar._store.fsutil.atomic_write — the shared crash-atomic file write.\n- rebar._store.lock.write_lock — the unified tickets write lock (context manager).\n- rebar._store.push.commit_and_push_tickets_branch(tracker, *, message=...) — commits all\n  pending tracker changes UNDER THE WRITE LOCK (+ rebase guard) then pushes.\n\n## Approach (pure conversion)\n1. projects_store._write_record: replace the hand-rolled mkstemp/fdopen/os.replace block\n   with `fsutil.atomic_write(path, json.dumps(record, indent=2, sort_keys=True) + \"\\n\")`.\n   Behavior-preserving: the on-disk bytes stay byte-identical, and the existing\n   `path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)` is KEPT before the call (atomic_write\n   requires the parent dir to already exist), so first-write still creates .bridge_state.\n   The module's read path stays stdlib-only standalone; the write path lazily imports the\n   rebar._store seams (only ever reached from the _lib_ops library layer, never from the\n   engine reconciler's read-only importers), and the module docstring is updated to state\n   this read-path-standalone / write-path-uses-seams split so the swap does not contradict\n   the documented invariant.\n2. Run the mutation under the lock AND publish it, both through existing seams, from the\n   single _lib_ops entry point that BOTH the CLI and the library route through\n   (bridge_projects_set / bridge_projects_remove -> set_project / remove_project): hold\n   `lock.write_lock(tracker)` around the read-modify-write call to set_project/remove_project\n   (so the RMW itself runs under the lock — no lost-update race), release it, then call\n   `push.commit_and_push_tickets_branch(tracker, message=\"bridge: update projects mapping\")`\n   (which re-acquires the same lock for the commit+push). No ad-hoc git; the read path\n   (load_mapping / read_projects) is untouched.\n3. Record the invariant (explicitly requested): add the two-part invariant to\n   docs/concurrency.md \"Mutating the tracker\" section — EVERY tickets-branch mutation runs\n   under write_lock AND auto-commits+publishes.\n\n## Explicitly OUT of scope (separate tickets)\n- Write-time project-key VALIDATION — separate ticket 209b (a distinct behavior addition,\n  not a seam conversion).\n- Any change to resolve_project / legacy_default (ticket a011).\n- Any modification of the shared seam or a new facade/helper over it (needs separate\n  approval).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] projects_store._write_record uses `fsutil.atomic_write` (not hand-rolled\n      mkstemp/os.replace) and keeps the `path.parent.mkdir(...)`; serialized bytes are\n      byte-identical to today, pinned by a RED-first test in\n      `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_projects_store_happy.py`.\n- [ ] A projects.json mutation runs its read-modify-write under `lock.write_lock` and is\n      then committed + pushed via `push.commit_and_push_tickets_branch(tracker, ...)` with no\n      ad-hoc git; verified by a seam-patched regression guard in\n      `tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_projects_happy.py`.\n- [ ] `docs/concurrency.md` \"Mutating the tracker\" section states the two-part invariant:\n      EVERY tickets-branch mutation runs under write_lock AND auto-commits+publishes.\n- [ ] No new commit/push/lock/atomic-write helper or facade is introduced; the existing\n      seams are used as-is (checked: `git diff` shows only inline seam call-sites added).\n\n## Testing\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_projects_store_happy.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_projects_store_heldout.py tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_projects_happy.py -q`\n- `make lint`\n- `make typecheck`\n\n## Sequencing\nEdits projects_store.py + docs/concurrency.md (+ tests); reuses push/fsutil/lock (no edit).\nDisjoint from A/C/D. Ticket 209b (key validation) and ticket E (parity conversion) both\nedit projects_store.py / the reconciler commit path and are sequenced AFTER this one.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/projects_store.py","reason":"Convert _write_record to fsutil.atomic_write; publish mutations via push.commit_and_push_tickets_branch"},{"path":"docs/concurrency.md","reason":"Record the two-part tickets-branch mutation invariant"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_projects_store_happy.py","reason":"Pin serialized bytes across atomic_write swap; assert commit_and_push invoked"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","6e0c-2639-3c03-417a"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"8f7603aa-cef5-4361-b811-2d28b64dd0c5","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"fea4-f98c-f1a2-4168","ticket_type":"task","title":"Bridge-state writes: adopt shared write_lock + commit+push + atomic_write seams (tickets-branch invariant)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["65d86ae7-94c0-457a-a562-be8b09f4fa85","35026b83-b3c4-4028-b1b0-4a40ef0effd0","9b5ecfd0-888c-41ab-9697-ca4cda12c40f","7c55243c-7584-4120-9441-1f0669dbea5c","657b4586-abde-4ea2-8aaa-14870ee4ae4b","02daa096-515c-4c97-b621-e8e8bb887e5b","ee0a456a-3775-468d-9242-39561852a085","9a25d5ec-b5d9-4bab-88fc-85f781abb29b","8f7603aa-cef5-4361-b811-2d28b64dd0c5","c23fa8d4-6c96-4224-9a7e-72cedad6d383","2209c64e-08bf-4403-921a-bf079d72b4dc","a2755f46-5a81-42b9-a48f-458f71faefdf","63672381-5842-4ef2-a4a1-9fd5bca7e0fa"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786816279497762001,"uuid":"303e5d66-7bcd-4f69-bd3e-8e6c581139c0"}